From 00a88a984db9f1568a12d89c48b5b2113c007f83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:34:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0089 -- fine-grained sub-phase breakdown of
 render_to_screen_pertick

Operator-directed follow-up to patch 0087: the horizontal-replication
fix cut render_to_screen_pertick from ~121ms to ~74ms/call but did not
explain where the remaining ~74ms goes. Instrument before guessing
again, same discipline that found patch 0087 itself.

Adds sub-phase brackets for every real step in render_to_screen()'s
own call chain: screen_overlay_vsync (the plugin-hook check,
construct_engine_overlay(), and vsync-set logic, before
gfxDriver->Render()), and inside Present() itself:
present_get_win_surface, present_sync_palette, present_flip_handling
(expected near-zero for this game, verified not assumed),
present_blit, and present_update_window (the actual push to the
display). Also breaks present_blit down further via manual microsecond
accumulation inside TryFastIntegerNearestBlit() itself (one
dos_port_tick_record() call per Present(), not per source row, to
avoid per-row RAII overhead across up to 240 rows/call):
fastblit_lock, fastblit_hreplicate, fastblit_vmemcpy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014hnodGZ6cg8CWuFXEDTsUq
